<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75808" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκέτι</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἔτι,</span></b> 
		Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>no more, no longer, no
			further</i>: and generally, <i>not now</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔπω</span> (not yet), freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i>, and 
				Att.
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκέτι πάμπαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.701
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκέτι πάγχυ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					19.343
				</span></i>
			; with a word between, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ πάμπαν ἔτι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					13.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ γὰρ ἔτι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.13
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				141
			</span></i>, etc.—Sts. reversely, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτ᾽ οὐκ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					161
				</span></i>
			, cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτ᾽ οὐδέν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1217
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτ᾽ οὐδείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					1177
				</span></i>
			.</div>
